shape: Directional/Twin (directional shape with twin flex, symmetrical from tip to tail)
camber type: Camber (most aggressive board bend for power, response, edge control, powerful turns, and poppy precision)
width options: Standard, Wide
inserts: The Channel (Burton Channel mounting system for fine-tuned stance width and location, compatible with most binding brands, best with Burton EST bindings)
available sizes: 150cm, 154cm, 156cm, 158cm, 162cm, 158cm Wide, 162cm Wide, 166cm Wide, 170cm Wide
laminate: 45° Carbon Highlights (tip to tail carbon layer with 45° angled fibres for reduced weight and fine-tuned torsional flex)
core: Super Fly II 700G Core with Dualzone EGD and Squeezebox
core detail: Stronger and lighter woods in specific areas for more pop and strength while reducing weight
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain aligned along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to rest of core for consistent edge hold and strength)
core sections: Squeezebox (thicker powerful sections combined with thinner flexible sections profiled throughout core for enhanced energy transfer, snappier and more stable)
edges: Frostbite Edges (extend out slightly underneath bindings for enhanced edge hold on hardpack and ice)
base: Sintered WFO (extra absorbent high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax for ultra durable base)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin reducing carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
tip/tail design: Pro-Tip (tip and tail taper out at points, reducing swing weight and promoting mobility)
flex treatment: Infinite Ride (boards overbuilt then broken down at factory for consistent pop and performance from day one to day 100)
also available as: Burton Custom Flying-V (more forgiving and versatile ride)
shipping restriction: Only available for shipping within Australia
